    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44570" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sŏdālĭcĭārĭus</span></b> 
			(<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sŏdālĭt-</span></b> ), a,
		um, adj.
		sodalicium, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to an
				associalion</i> or <i>fellowship</i>, only as <i>subst.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sŏdālĭcĭārĭus</span></b> ,
				ii, m., one who is bound to another by
			fellowship, <i>a comrade</i>, <i>bosomfriend</i>, <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell.
			4794</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sŏdālĭcĭ-ārĭa</span></b> ,
				ae, f.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">SODALICIARIA CONSILII BONI,</span>”
				<i>a companion</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 4644</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
